// Coverage: a 'chords { }' block — symbolic chord entry displayed as chord
// symbols above the staff, aligned by timing to the melody. Roots auto-name from
// root+quality (c -> "C", a:m -> "Am"); mid-bar changes land at their musical
// moment. Also exercises a MULTI-TOKEN quality (g:m7.5- -> "Gm7♭5") and the
// chord-row CLEARANCE over a tall chord the wide symbol overhangs (the last
// beat's <c ees ges bes> reaches above the staff, so the whole row is raised to
// clear it). Verified against LilyPond \chords / \chordmode.
// LILYPOND-REF: ly/engraver-init.ly ChordNames; scm/chord-entry.scm;
// lily/axis-group-interface.cc (skyline-spaced ChordNames group).
// Known simplification: names are plain text (Lily# style), not LilyPond's
// superscript/triangle typography.
title "Chord names"
key c major
part m { clef treble }
section Main {
  m {
    time 4/4
    c4 d e f | g a b <c ees ges bes> |
  }
  chords {
    c2 a2:m | f2 g2:m7.5- |
  }
}
form main { Main }
score main "chordnames" { staff m }
